    <fr:title text="Terminal Object">Terminal Object</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <fr:p>An object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c]]></fr:tex> in a category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> is <fr:em>terminal</fr:em> if there is a unique morphism from any other object into it.</fr:p>
    <fr:p>Because terminal objects are unique up to unique isomorphism (as are all universal objects) we often just write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\top ]]></fr:tex> to refer to the terminal object. Likewise, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[! : d \to  \top ]]></fr:tex> refers to the unique morphism into <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\top ]]></fr:tex>.</fr:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
